# title: Combat guard
# description: Visits its waypoints and hunts the hostile mobs it finds with a sword, fetches another sword when one breaks, and goes to the charger when its power is low and back to exactly where it was.
# Setup
#  1. Waypoints tab: save the posts it visits (post1, post2 ... in route below), "charger"
#     (the robot stands on a charger) and, if you want spare swords, "armory" (the robot
#     in front of a chest of swords, facing the chest). Save them with the robot standing
#     at each place facing the way it should face. Set armory = "" for none.
#  2. Put a sword in the robot's storage. When it breaks the robot uses the next one it
#     has; when it has none it walks to the armory and takes one out of the chest.
#  3. monsters is a list of entity names separated by commas, without spaces: the
#     hostile mobs of Mobs Monster and of MineClone / VoxeLibre / Mineclonia. Add the
#     names of your own (the entity front query tells a name: chat entity front).
#
# Players: a robot with a Combat Upgrade can hit players (never its owner, and only where
# pvp is on). Put names in enemies, "griefer,thief", and with one Combat Upgrade they
# are hunted like the monsters. With two or more upgrades the punch reaches one block
# further for each, so the robot hits while it is still walking up to its target.
use waypoint
use pathfind
use strings

# --- settings ---
set route = "post1,post2"
set charger = "charger"
set armory = "armory"
set weapon = "group:sword"
set low_power = 30
set full_power = 95
set monsters = "mobs_monster:dirt_monster,mobs_monster:stone_monster,mobs_monster:sand_monster,mobs_monster:tree_monster,mobs_monster:mese_monster,mobs_monster:spider,mobs_monster:oerkki,mobs_monster:dungeon_master,mobs_monster:lava_flan,mobs_mc:zombie,mobs_mc:husk,mobs_mc:drowned,mobs_mc:skeleton,mobs_mc:stray,mobs_mc:spider,mobs_mc:cave_spider,mobs_mc:creeper,mobs_mc:witch,mobs_mc:slime_big,mobs_mc:slime_small,mobs_mc:silverfish,mobs_mc:pillager"
set enemies = ""

# whom it fights: the monsters, and the players in enemies when it has a Combat Upgrade
set combat = upgrade_count "combat"
set targets = monsters
if combat >= 1 and length enemies > 0
  set targets = monsters + "," + enemies

# take a sword out of the armory chest and come back to where I was
fn fetch_weapon
  set known = call waypoint.has armory
  if not known
    return false
  call waypoint.save "back"
  set arrived = call waypoint.go_face armory
  if arrived = 0
    pull weapon
  call waypoint.go_face "back"
  return contains weapon

# is there a sword in storage (fetched when not)
fn armed
  if contains weapon
    return true
  set got = call fetch_weapon
  return got

# hit what is in front until it is gone, the swords are gone or the power is low
fn swing seen
  loop entity front = seen and counter < 100 and battery_level >= low_power
    set ready = call armed
    if not ready
      break
    punch front weapon

# look all around: hit what is hostile next to me; true when it fought
fn fight
  set fought = false
  repeat 4
    set seen = entity front
    if seen != ""
      set hostile = call strings.has_part targets "," seen
      if hostile
        call swing seen
        set fought = true
    turn right
  return fought

# the name of the nearest hostile entity in sight, "" when there is none
fn nearest
  set total = call strings.parts targets ","
  set best = ""
  set best_steps = 0
  set index = 1
  loop index <= total
    set kind = call strings.split targets "," index
    set steps = call pathfind.start_entity kind
    if steps >= 0 and (best = "" or steps < best_steps)
      set best = kind
      set best_steps = steps
    add index 1
  call pathfind.cancel
  return best

# walk up to the nearest entity of that name (hitting on the way with more Combat Upgrades)
fn approach kind
  set left = call pathfind.start_entity kind
  loop left > 0 and battery_level >= low_power
    set left = call pathfind.step
    if combat > 1 and contains weapon
      punch front weapon

# one round: find a hostile, walk up to it and fight it; false when there was none
fn hunt
  set target = call nearest
  if target = ""
    return false
  call approach target
  call fight
  return true

# power is low: remember the spot and the facing, charge, and come back to exactly there
fn recharge
  call waypoint.save "work"
  call waypoint.go_face charger
  loop battery_level < full_power
    wait 100
  call waypoint.go_face "work"

set posts = call strings.parts route ","
set visit = 1
forever
  if battery_level < low_power
    call recharge
  set post = call strings.split route "," visit
  call waypoint.go_face post
  # fight what is around, one after the other
  set found = true
  loop found and battery_level >= low_power
    set found = call hunt
  wait 20
  add visit 1
  if visit > posts
    set visit = 1
